OL,3,GNEWSAFootballer to fund former club's
OL,4,Asuicide campaign
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former Oxford United player will
OL,7,Fcontinue to fund its suicide prevention
OL,8,Fcampaign, despite leaving the club over
OL,9,Fthe summer.
OL,11,FFormer Yellows midfielder Will Vaulks
OL,12,Fsigned for his boyhood club Tranmere
OL,13,FRovers in August, bringing an end to
OL,14,Fhis two year spell at the Kassam.
OL,16,FDuring his time in the city, the
OL,17,F32-year-old spearheaded the club's Can
OL,18,FWe Talk? campaign, focusing on mental
OL,19,Fhealth awareness in the workplace.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
